whois — provenance note
=======================

Kept as a module-local NOTICE (same placement as the sibling `ocsp`/`dns`/
`rdap` modules, which document the same live-capture reasoning).

Provenance
----------

whois — clean-room implementation from RFC 3912 plus the documented IANA and
registry line conventions; no third-party source was ported or copied.

`modules/whois/src/goldens.zig` (added 2026-08-01) holds two real WHOIS
replies captured live over port 43: IANA's answer for `com` (bare `\n` line
endings) and Verisign's `.com` registry answer for `domain example.com`
(real CRLF). See that file's own doc comment for the capture recipe and for
what the real replies exercise that the hand-typed fixtures in `root.zig`
could not — principally real line-ending and key-prefix shapes, and the
genuine referral cycle that arises because `example.com` is IANA-reserved,
so the registry's reply points back at `whois.iana.org`.

Attribution for the captured replies: NONE required, by the same reasoning
`ocsp`'s NOTICE gives for its live CA captures (root NOTICE §0's
black-box-oracle relationship): no third-party source or design was
consulted, only the observable port-43 output of public registries answering
a stock RFC 3912 query — protocol structure plus already-published registry
facts, not copyrightable expression. Registry boilerplate (the NOTICE and
TERMS-OF-USE prose each reply carries) is retained verbatim in the captured
bytes because a WHOIS reply is only a faithful fixture if it is unmodified;
it is not asserted against and carries no condition this repository
redistributes under. No root NOTICE change accompanies this addition.

No GPL/LGPL/AGPL source was consulted or copied anywhere in this module.
